From: ffmpeggui maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/mediacodecenc: avoid flushing NDK encoders for extradata

MediaCodec only defines flush recovery for decoders. Encoder flush behavior is
undefined, and c2.google.avc.encoder/c2.google.hevc.encoder on Tensor G5 enter
an error state after the synchronous global-header probe queues a dummy frame,
queues EOS, and flushes the encoder. The following real frame is rejected with
Codec2 status 95 and AVERROR_EXTERNAL.

The existing extract_extradata bitstream filter already handles codec config
when async NDK mode skips this probe. Use the same path for synchronous NDK
encoding, avoiding the unsupported encoder flush while preserving the existing
JNI behavior.

The issue reproduces on a Pixel 10 Pro XL / Tensor G5 running Android 17 when
writing H.264 or HEVC to MP4 or Matroska. Raw elementary streams are unaffected.
---
 libavcodec/mediacodecenc.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libavcodec/mediacodecenc.c b/libavcodec/mediacodecenc.c
index 507c48df9c..aade091cf4 100644
--- a/libavcodec/mediacodecenc.c
+++ b/libavcodec/mediacodecenc.c
@@ -947,7 +947,7 @@ static int mediacodec_generate_extradata(AVCodecContext *avctx)
         return 0;
 
     // Send dummy frame and receive a packet doesn't work in async mode
-    if (s->async_mode || !s->extract_extradata) {
+    if (s->async_mode || !s->extract_extradata || s->use_ndk_codec) {
         av_log(avctx, AV_LOG_WARNING,
                "Mediacodec encoder doesn't support AV_CODEC_FLAG_GLOBAL_HEADER. "
                "Use extract_extradata bsf when necessary.\n");
-- 
